  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">CO-Oxfam Nigeria</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project comes from the solicited call on behalf of the German Federal Ministry for Economic Cooperation and Development (BMZ),the Deutsche Gesellschaft f&#xfc;r Internationale Zusammenarbeit (GIZ) GmbH is implementing the Programme, &#x2018;Social and EconomicParticipation of Returnees, IDPs and Host Population in North-East Nigeria&#x2019; (SEPIN). The main objective of the programme is to improve the economic and social participation of returnees, internally displaced persons, and vulnerable members of host communities in Adamawa State in a gender responsive way.
This call therefore seeks for expression of interest to support and facilitate gender responsive andinclusive community development planning processes in the 16 wards of Michika Local Government Area ofAdamawa State, develop a harmonized Local Government Development Plan for Michika LGA using the Ward Development Plans, conduct a sector analysis for the LGA Development Plan, Cost the LGA Development Plan, include a basic M&lt;(&gt;&amp;&lt;)&gt;E framework for internal and external monitoring of implementation of the plan and build capacity of local government officials in planning, budgeting and implementation of the development plansamongst other capacity development measures, and support the communities to implement a fewprojects contained in the Ward Development Plans.</narrative>
  </description>
